{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042294-fabricating-sympathy-with-life-magic","id":1042294,"title":"Fabricating Sympathy with Life Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-02T02:14:36-08:00","id":1042294,"title":"Fabricating Sympathy with Life Magic","content":"So I'd like to see if this would fly with you folks...<br /> <br /> My Thyrsus player's objective is to keep tabs on another person. Monitor and possibly cast Sympathetic magic on them.<br /> <br /> 1. He casts 'Many Faces' (Life 3) to take on his target's appearance, scent, health condition, and age. On an anatomical and physiological level they are identical.<br /> <br /> 2. He preserves a lock of his own transformed hair, or a patch of skin, or a tooth. The body part remains transformed on Indefinite Duration.<br /> <br /> Provided the appropriate dots in Space, can he use the 'fabricated' body part as a Sympathetic Yantra? If so, what do you think the Sympathetic strength be?<br /> <br /> Feel free to share a link if this has been discussed elsewhere in the forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:32:13-08:00","id":1042303,"title":"","content":"As a yantra? Sure, representational sympathy. Even <i>drawings </i>can be used as Yantras.<br /> Would this actually provide a sympathetic connection to use for the casting? Not in the slightest.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that sympathetic casting requires two separate, unrelated things:<br /> <br /> 1) A sympathetic connection to the subject<br /> 2) A sympathy yantra.<br /> <br /> The second one is incredibly easy to get, using this Life transformation scheme is actually a really convoluted way to go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 02-02-2017, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:34:24-08:00","id":1042305,"title":"","content":"Can Many Faces be used to copy someone that precisely in the first place? Does sympathy follow genetics?<br /> <br /> Even after those, I don't think the separated body part would stay transformed. The spell targeted the mage as a whole, so either the body part reverts upon separation or it reverts together with the rest of the mage when the spell expires.<br /> <br /> Does the player want to do the whole thing in total secret, without the victim knowing? If the subject is not a mage, then he could just cast any spell on them from afar, which nets the Thyrsus a Weak connection. The Thyrsus may then strengthen it with Space magic.<br /> <br /> Or, if the Thyrsus has time, they could disguise themselves with Many Faces to appear as a completely different person and approach the subject, gradually building both a mundane connection and a magical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:34:53-08:00","id":1042306,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's a Representation Yantra with no Sympathetic connection to the target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:34:08-08:00","id":1042435,"title":"","content":"I would rule it an specially good representation Yantra and grant maybe one or two extra dice, although when using it for sympathetic range that would be useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T08:52:12-08:00","id":1042449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042294-fabricating-sympathy-with-life-magic?p=1042435#post1042435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rule it an specially good representation Yantra and grant maybe one or two extra dice, although when using it for sympathetic range that would be useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Representational Yantras grants <s>zero dice</s> one die by definition though. Adding extra dice would be treating it as a different type of yantra, that's the only mechanical distinction between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 02-02-2017, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T09:11:41-08:00","id":1042464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042294-fabricating-sympathy-with-life-magic?p=1042449#post1042449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Representational Yantras grant zero dice by definition though. Adding extra dice would be treating it as a different type of yantra, that's the only mechanical distinction between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just checked the Sympathetic Yantras and I'd say that if you shapeshifted into and exact replica of the subject that would count as Material Yantra, considering a recent picture works. I would even give you a die bonus for going to the trouble of actually &quot;embodying&quot; the subject. But again, this is moot when you are using sympathetic range, unless you use another Sympathetic Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:56:00-08:00","id":1042514,"title":"","content":"Just reviewed all of the sympathy Yantra stuff again. I was mistakenly referring to Symbolic as Representational.<br /> Honestly I could see arguments for this falling under any of the three categories, it really comes down to ST preference. <br /> But no sympathetic connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T21:25:56-08:00","id":1042793,"title":"","content":"Why not just make some sort of biological agent that you have strong sympathy with (you're it's creator afterall) and then just infect whoever you want to create sympathy with.<br /> <br /> Make it so the organism intertwines with the person on enough of a level that affecting the agent affects the person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T22:31:46-08:00","id":1042819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cantankerous Bees</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042294-fabricating-sympathy-with-life-magic?p=1042793#post1042793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it so the organism intertwines with the person on enough of a level that affecting the agent affects the person.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good approach. This last part isn't even necessary, open a scrying window to the agent and you should be able to target the person via Remote Sensory range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T22:36:58-08:00","id":1042820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cantankerous Bees</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1042294-fabricating-sympathy-with-life-magic?p=1042793#post1042793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it so the organism intertwines with the person on enough of a level that affecting the agent affects the person.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Medium sympathy suffices then you can manage this with literally any spell and a half-decent drawing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}